# Raw JSONL logs — never committed. Benches summarise into docs/bench-results-*.md,
# and everything else that emits JSONL is a trace or a scratch artifact.
#
# By filetype, not by filename. This was `scripts/bench_raw_*.jsonl`, which held
# only because every JSONL on disk happened to match that one pattern: a bench
# variant writing elsewhere, or any tool emitting a trace, landed as untracked and
# was one `git add -A` from being committed. Nothing is tracked as JSONL today, so
# this ignores no existing file.
#
# If a JSONL ever genuinely belongs in the repo (a fixture, say), add a negation
# beside this line — `!scripts/bench_fixtures/whatever.jsonl` — rather than reaching
# for `git add -f`, so the exception is visible to the next person.
*.jsonl
docs/model-cache.md

# dflash diagnostics output
.artifacts/